  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-{390}^{∘}?$\n\nI. $-{30}^{∘}$\n\nII. ${305}^{∘}$\n\nIII. $-{750}^{∘}$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{390}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{390}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-{30}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\n- $-{390}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={330}^{∘}$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${330}^{∘}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{390}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{390}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{750}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only $-{30}^{∘}$ and $-{750}^{∘}$ are coterminal with $-{390}^{∘}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only.",
